  "note": "Patcher matrix for B184, built from main at ee4000f. Seeded per variant from the B181 matrix outputs. Seeding matters here beyond convenience: VF2 builds INHERIT assets from the seed, so a seed older than the previous release silently drops the art that release added, and the build still reports success. Each of the 32 seed directories was checked INDIVIDUALLY against the runtime payload contract (wc.dat, the Original Virtual Families 2 Assets folder, and a linked exe) rather than trusting the newest matching prefix, because an interrupted run leaves a directory that satisfies none of them and the directory is created before anything links. B184 EXISTS BECAUSE B183 SHIPPED TWELVE FEATURES SHORT: it was exported by calling work/export_offline_patch_bundle.py directly instead of work/export_release_bundle.py, so the wrapper's guards never ran -- one of which exists precisely to refuse a build whose overlays would be silently absent. No release config existed for B182 or B183, which is the likely reason the wrapper was bypassed at all. This file is the input that wrapper requires. The B181 seeds must NOT be moved, renamed or deleted: they are inputs to this build, not stale outputs. NOTE ON THE SEED EXECUTABLES: every one of the 32 B181-era overlays predates the startup-crash fix and carries the faulty byte sequence. The seeds supply ASSETS; the executables must be rebuilt from current main, and each rebuilt overlay verified individually (faulty 84c0590f85 absent, fixed 84c05974065b present). Nothing anywhere in the release path inspects overlay bytes, so that check is the only thing preventing a guard-passing release from shipping the crash.",
